{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 25, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The land of the rising sun. It's a phrase that conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and serene gardens – and it absolutely delivers on all fronts! I just returned from a whirlwind trip, and I'm already dreaming of going back.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way possible. Neon lights, incredible food stalls (ramen, sushi, takoyaki – I tried it all!), and the organized chaos of Shibuya Crossing were unforgettable. I spent days exploring vibrant neighborhoods like Harajuku and Shinjuku, soaking up the unique street style and quirky shops.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took a bullet train to Kyoto, a complete contrast. Here, the pace slowed, and the focus shifted to history and tradition. Visiting Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of red torii gates was breathtaking. I wandered through the enchanting Arashiyama Bamboo Grove and found peace in the meticulously manicured gardens of Kinkaku-ji (the Golden Pavilion).\n\nThe food was consistently amazing. From delicate matcha sweets to savory okonomiyaki, every meal was an adventure. And the people? Incredibly polite and helpful, even with my limited Japanese.\n\nJapan is a country of contrasts, a place where ancient traditions seamlessly blend with modern innovation. It’s a trip that truly feeds the soul, and I can't recommend it enough.  Sayonara for now, Japan!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0012646066024899483}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.14694757759571075}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0011703077470883727}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.11968507617712021}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.10784334689378738}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.18911860883235931}